E["npc:bloodmage-drazial"] = {t="npc",n="Bloodmage Drazial",z="blastedlands",s="Bloodmage Drazial is a blood elf practitioner of arcane and blood magic camped in the northern reaches of the Blasted Lands. Alongside his sister Lynnore, he studies the native beasts of the red wastes to craft potent alchemical concoctions for traveling adventurers.",h="Bloodmage Drazial is a blood elf practitioner of arcane and blood magic camped in the northern reaches of the...",sec={{t="Alchemical Studies in the Red Wastes",b="Perched near the northern pass where the Swamp of Sorrows gives way to the Blasted Lands, Bloodmage Drazial pursues a peculiar brand of magic. While many high elves shun the forbidden arts or despair over Quel'Thalas, Drazial and his sister Lynnore harness blood magic to harvest power from the harsh environment. The blighted fauna of the wastes—scorpoks, snickerfangs, and blasted boars—absorb unusual magical energies through their diet and survival in the crimson soil. By harvesting specific organs and tissues from these creatures, Drazial brews volatile concoctions that grant immense bursts of physical strength, agility, and endurance.",sp=0},{t="An Independent Supplier",b="Unlike many factional agents stationed in the Blasted Lands, Drazial operates with practical detachment. He holds no official allegiance to either the Alliance or the Horde, choosing instead to trade his alchemical expertise to anyone hardy enough to brave the wasteland and gather the raw ingredients he requires. As long as travelers bring him the organs of the local predators, Drazial is content to keep his cauldrons bubbling.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Bloodmage Drazial?",a="Bloodmage Drazial is a blood elf mage stationed near the northern entrance of the Blasted Lands. Together with his sister Lynnore, he studies the local wildlife and brews powerful alchemical reagents using parts collected from the area's corrupted beasts.",al={"who is drazial","drazial lore","bloodmage drazial npc"}},{q="Why is Drazial collecting animal parts?",a="The creatures of the Blasted Lands have adapted to survive on blighted, magically charged terrain. Drazial uses the potent internal organs of boars, hyenas, scorpions, and basilisks to concoct specialized elixirs that bolster a warrior's physical prowess.",al={"why does drazial want boar lungs","drazial quest items","drazial animal organs"}},{q="Does Drazial work for the Alliance or the Horde?",a="Drazial is neutral toward both factions. He and Lynnore do not concern themselves with the war between Stormwind and the Horde, readily dealing with any adventurer willing to supply their magical and alchemical research.",al={"drazial faction","is drazial horde or alliance","can alliance talk to drazial"}},{q="Who is the other blood elf camped with him?",a="The elf beside him is his sister, Bloodmage Lynnore. Together, the siblings practice blood magic and brew distinct concoctions from the various beasts roaming the Blasted Lands.",al={"drazial companion","who is with drazial","lynnore"}}},ang={["class:Mage"]="Drazial represents the controversial divergence of the blood elves, openly utilizing blood magic and biological reagents to synthesize arcane enhancements rather than relying strictly on traditional Kirin Tor spellcraft."},kw={"blasted boar","blasted lands","bloodmage","concoctions","drazial","lynnore","scorpok","snickerfang"},rel={"zone:blastedlands","topic:alliance","topic:horde"},src={"Bloodmage Drazial"}}
E["npc:bloodmage-lynnore"] = {t="npc",n="Bloodmage Lynnore",z="blastedlands",s="Bloodmage Lynnore is a blood elf practitioner of forbidden blood magic camped with her brother Drazial near the northern entrance to the Blasted Lands. She assists adventurers by concocting potent alchemical draughts from the organs of local beasts.",h="Bloodmage Lynnore is a blood elf practitioner of forbidden blood magic camped with her brother Drazial near...",sec={{t="Master of Blood Magic",b="Camped near the northern entrance to the Blasted Lands alongside her brother Drazial, Bloodmage Lynnore is one of the exceptionally rare elven practitioners of blood magic found in the Eastern Kingdoms. Unperturbed by the harsh and corrupting landscape of the Blasted Lands, she studies the latent arcane and vital energies coursing through native beasts. Travelers who bring her the brains and gizzards of local fauna find that she can distill these gruesome reagents into specialized elixirs granting profound enhancements to intellect and spirit.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Bloodmage Lynnore?",a="Bloodmage Lynnore is a blood elf blood mage camped near the northern entrance to the Blasted Lands. She serves as a quest giver and alchemical specialist, offering powerful stat-enhancing concoctions in exchange for beast parts.",al={"who is lynnore","bloodmage lynnore lore","lynnore blasted lands"}},{q="Where can Bloodmage Lynnore be found?",a="She makes her camp with her brother, Bloodmage Drazial, near the northern entrance to the Blasted Lands, where the pass from the Swamp of Sorrows opens onto the wastes.",al={"lynnore location","where is lynnore","how to find bloodmage lynnore"}},{q="What concoctions does she brew?",a="Lynnore uses parts scavenged from the local wildlife—such as basilisk brains, vulture gizzards, and snickerfang jowls—to brew rare tonics like the Cerebral Cortex Compound and Gizzard Gum, which grant prolonged enhancements to intellect and spirit.",al={"lynnore buffs","blasted lands consumables","cerebral cortex compound"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Lynnore acts as a valuable tactical contact in the Blasted Lands, trading unique alchemical reagents and offering dark arcane expertise to advance Horde power against local demonic threats.",["class:Mage"]="For mages fascinated by unconventional spellcraft, Lynnore represents an elusive and controversial branch of arcane philosophy that manipulates vital essence rather than conventional ley energies."},kw={"blasted lands","blood magic","bloodmage lynnore","cerebral cortex compound","dreadmaul furnace","gizzard gum","loramus thalipedes","lynnore"},rel={"zone:blastedlands","npc:loramus-thalipedes","topic:horde"},src={"Bloodmage Lynnore"}}
E["npc:thadius-grimshade"] = {t="npc",n="Thadius Grimshade",z="blastedlands",s="Thadius Grimshade is a Wildhammer dwarf diviner dwelling within the mage tower of Nethergarde Keep in the Blasted Lands. Though he parted ways with Aerie Peak long ago to study esoteric and darker magical arts, he remains loyal to his kin at heart.",h="Thadius Grimshade is a Wildhammer dwarf diviner dwelling within the mage tower of Nethergarde Keep in the...",sec={{t="A Wildhammer in the Wastes",b="Unlike most Wildhammer dwarves who prefer the open skies and roaring winds of the Hinterlands, Thadius Grimshade makes his home inside Nethergarde Keep. Driven by a thirst for arcane divination and darker mystic lore, he relocated to the edge of the tainted Blasted Lands to pursue his esoteric studies. Despite his brooding discipline and separation from his clan, he retains a deep fondness for his homeland and gryphonkind, offering his rare scrying talents to those who come seeking aid on behalf of Aerie Peak.",sp=0},{t="The Price of Divination",b="When Gryphon Master Talonaxe seeks to locate the captured gryphon Sharpbeak, Thadius is called upon to perform a divination ritual using one of the beast's feathers. His magical insight does not come without a price: Thadius demands the medallion worn by the troll necromancer Nekrum Gutchewer. Seeking to unlock its secret of unnatural longevity while evading its harmful corruptions, he takes the artifact in exchange for piercing the veil of Jintha'Alor and revealing where Sharpbeak is held.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Thadius Grimshade?",a="He is an eccentric Wildhammer dwarf mage and diviner stationed in Nethergarde Keep. He left his mountain home to pursue darker, unorthodox magical arts far to the south.",al={"thadius grimshade","who is thadius","thadius npc"}},{q="Where can Thadius Grimshade be found?",a="He resides inside the high wizard tower of Nethergarde Keep, an Alliance stronghold situated in the northern reaches of the Blasted Lands.",al={"thadius location","where is thadius grimshade","thadius blasted lands"}},{q="Why does he want Nekrum's Medallion?",a="Thadius wishes to study the medallion carried by Nekrum Gutchewer to decipher how its magical power grants long life, hoping to claim that longevity without succumbing to its sinister side effects.",al={"nekrums medallion thadius","why thadius wants medallion","nekrum gutchewer medallion"}},{q="How does he help find Sharpbeak?",a="Using a feather shed by the lost gryphon and the power fueled by Nekrum's Medallion, Thadius conducts a scrying ritual that reveals Sharpbeak is imprisoned at the heights of Jintha'Alor in the Hinterlands.",al={"thadius sharpbeak","divining sharpbeak","finding sharpbeak quest"},sp=1}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="Fellow dwarves will find Thadius an oddity among Wildhammers; rather than soaring on gryphons, he spends his years buried in arcane study within a human fortress.",["class:Mage"]="Mages visiting Nethergarde will recognize Thadius as a practitioner of rare and esoteric divination methods, willing to examine troll relics to master longevity magic."},kw={"blasted lands","diviner","nekrum gutchewer","nethergarde keep","sharpbeak","thadius grimshade","wildhammer"},rel={"subzone:nethergarde-keep","zone:blastedlands","zone:hinterlands","topic:dwarf"},src={"Thadius Grimshade"}}
E["subzone:dark-portal"] = {t="subzone",n="Dark Portal",z="blastedlands",s="The Dark Portal is a monumental stone gateway standing at the southern rim of the Blasted Lands. First torn open through the combined sorcery of Medivh and Gul'dan, it served as the fateful conduit that brought the Old Horde into Azeroth, initiating the First War.",h="The Dark Portal is a monumental stone gateway standing at the southern rim of the Blasted Lands.",sec={{t="A Rift Across Realities",b="Before its opening, this region was part of the Black Morass, a sodden wetland that stretched across the south. That changed when Medivh, possessed by Sargeras, joined his Tirisfal magics with the fel sorcery of Gul'dan on Draenor. The ritual drained untold lives and tore the fabric of reality apart. The Old Horde raised massive stone architecture to anchor the rift, marching armies through its threshold to shatter the Kingdom of Stormwind in the First War. The portal's fel emanations fundamentally corrupted the surrounding terrain, reducing lush marshes to the red, petrified wastes seen today.",sp=0},{t="Dormant Vigilance",b="Following the Alliance of Lordaeron's victory in the Second War, Archmage Khadgar shattered the physical stone frame with powerful magics, hoping to sever Draenor forever. However, the dimensional tear beneath proved functionally indestructible. The Alliance erected Nethergarde Keep nearby to watch the scar, while demons and remnants of the Shadow Council continue to slink through the blasted caldera. Today the gateway stands reassembled yet dormant, a silent scar between worlds that neither side dares abandon.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Can you walk through the Dark Portal right now?",a="No. The gateway's stone frame stands intact, but the rift within is dormant. No traveler can cross the threshold at this time.",al={"can i enter the dark portal","is dark portal open","portal to outland"}},{q="Who originally built the Dark Portal?",a="It was created through a joint ritual between the human Guardian Medivh on Azeroth and the warlock Gul'dan on the dying world of Draenor, orchestrating the invasion that ignited the First War.",al={"who created dark portal","medivh guldan portal","dark portal creators"}},{q="Why does Nethergarde Keep watch over it?",a="After Archmage Khadgar shattered the portal's initial frame after the Second War, he convinced the Alliance to keep watch over its ruins. Nethergarde Keep was founded by the Alliance to maintain a permanent watch over the site in case threats emerged again.",al={"why is nethergarde keep here","nethergarde portal watch","why nethergarde"}},{q="Why is the ground around the portal red and barren?",a="The Blasted Lands were once a fertile swamp known as the Black Morass. The vast fel energies required to breach reality, coupled with the corruption flowing from Draenor and demonic beasts, poisoned the soil and petrified the ecosystem.",al={"why are blasted lands dead","portal corruption","why is blasted lands red"}}},ang={["race:Orc"]="The portal is the painful threshold of your people's past—the gate through which the Old Horde marched in thrall to demonic masters, abandoning their ancestral homeland for war.",["faction:Alliance"]="For the Alliance, the portal is a solemn monument to the First War and the fall of ancient Stormwind, necessitating the perpetual vigil held by the mages of Nethergarde."},kw={"black morass","blasted lands","dark portal","draenor","great portal","guldan","khadgar","medivh"},rel={"zone:blastedlands","subzone:nethergarde-keep","topic:medivh","topic:old-horde","topic:first-war","topic:second-war","topic:burning-legion","topic:alliance-of-lordaeron"},src={"Dark Portal"}}
E["subzone:dreadmaul-post"] = {t="subzone",n="Dreadmaul Post",z="blastedlands",s="Dreadmaul Post is an entrenched ogre settlement situated in the scorched wastes of the Blasted Lands. Established by the Dreadmaul clan, this mound serves as a fortified redoubt near the Dark Portal where ogres have lingered since their arrival from Draenor. Travelers passing through the region must contend with these fierce brutes and the treacherous terrain surrounding their encampment.",h="Dreadmaul Post is an entrenched ogre settlement situated in the scorched wastes of the Blasted Lands.",sec={{t="Remnants of Draenor",b="When the Horde surged through the Dark Portal in decades past, clans of ogres marched alongside them into Azeroth. The Dreadmaul clan chose to dig in near the gateway itself, raising crude stone mounds and earthworks across the red wastes of the Blasted Lands. Dreadmaul Post stands as one of their primary outposts, maintaining a firm grip over the badlands and clashing with wandering beasts and any travelers foolish enough to draw near their territory.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who lives at Dreadmaul Post?",a="Dreadmaul Post is inhabited by the Dreadmaul clan of ogres. These hulking brutes crossed over from Draenor through the Dark Portal during the wars and established a permanent foothold in the desolate crags of the Blasted Lands.",al={"who is at dreadmaul post","dreadmaul post inhabitants","dreadmaul ogres"}},{q="Why are the ogres still in the Blasted Lands?",a="Following the Old Horde's collapse and the sealing of the Dark Portal, many ogres scattered across Azeroth. The Dreadmaul clan, however, stayed close to their original entry point, making the scarred, desolate expanse around the dormant rift their home.",al={"why dreadmaul here","ogres blasted lands","why ogres near portal"}},{q="Who else wanders the area near the post?",a="Aside from the ogres themselves, fierce local predators like scorpid and basilisks wander the red desert near Dreadmaul Post.",al={"draenei blasted lands","who is near dreadmaul","creatures dreadmaul post"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Although ogres once fought alongside the Old Horde, wild clans like the Dreadmaul have long severed ties with Thrall's new order, viewing all travelers as hostile invaders.",["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance scouts monitoring the Dark Portal, the Dreadmaul ogres represent an entrenched, violent hazard that complicates any patrol through the southern reaches of the continent."},kw={"blasted lands","dark portal","dreadmaul","dreadmaul post","ogre mound","ogres"},rel={"zone:blastedlands","subzone:dark-portal","subzone:maul-subzone"},src={"Dreadmaul Post"}}
E["subzone:garrison-armory"] = {t="subzone",n="Garrison Armory",z="blastedlands",s="The Garrison Armory is an Alliance mining operation carved into the hills southwest of Nethergarde Keep in the Blasted Lands. Miners and engineers work the underground veins to harvest valuable minerals, sustaining the lonely fortress and shipping raw wealth back to Stormwind. It forms a crucial industrial lifeline in an otherwise blasted, barren wilderness.",h="The Garrison Armory is an Alliance mining operation carved into the hills southwest of Nethergarde Keep in...",sec={{t="A Lifeline in the Red Wastes",b="Maintaining a permanent military garrison in the arid wastes of the Blasted Lands requires constant supply, and Nethergarde Keep cannot rely purely on long supply trains from Stormwind. The Garrison Armory serves as the keep's primary industrial excavation. Nethergarde miners, overseen by foremen and assisted by engineers, work these subterranean shafts to pull valuable minerals from the earth. The ore extracted here is utilized directly by Nethergarde's smiths and fortifications or hauled back to the capital in exchange for the foodstuffs, tools, and provisions the fortress needs to maintain its vigil over the Dark Portal.",sp=0},{t="Vulnerable Industry",b="Because the armory sits away from the main walls of Nethergarde Keep, the excavation remains exposed to the harsh perils of the red desert. Trolls, ogres, and wild beasts prowl the surrounding crags, while agents of the Horde keep a close eye on Nethergarde's mining output. The workforce within the tunnels operates under armed guard, knowing that any disruption to the armory directly threatens Nethergarde's ability to maintain its watch over the blasted frontier.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Garrison Armory used for?",a="The Garrison Armory is an Alliance mining complex operated by Nethergarde Keep. Workers extract metal and minerals underground to maintain the fortress and trade back to Stormwind for essential food and equipment.",al={"garrison armory purpose","what is this mine","why is there a mine here"}},{q="Who works in the armory?",a="The mine is staffed by Nethergarde miners, engineers, and foremen affiliated with the Alliance. They work to excavate ore deposits and maintain the shafts beneath the supervision of Nethergarde's command.",al={"who is inside","armory npcs","garrison miners"}},{q="Why does Nethergarde Keep need this mine?",a="Nethergarde Keep sits isolated in the desolate Blasted Lands, making regular supply lines difficult. By extracting its own metals, the fortress can repair gear, reinforce defenses, and trade excess raw materials to Stormwind in exchange for vital survival supplies.",al={"why nethergarde needs it","armory importance","nethergarde resources"}},{q="Can Horde players enter the Garrison Armory?",a="The armory is occupied by hostile Alliance workers and guards, but Horde adventurers frequently brave the depths to claim the rich ore veins buried within the mine shafts.",al={"can horde go here","horde in garrison armory","is it safe for horde"}}},ang={["profession:Mining"]="The shafts of the Garrison Armory hold valuable mineral veins carved out of the rugged Blasted Lands stone, making it a contested subterranean quarry.",["faction:Alliance"]="The Armory's workforce labors constantly to ensure Nethergarde Keep remains supplied with weapons, armor, and trade goods to hold its lonely watch."},kw={"blasted lands","garrison armory","mine","nethergarde","nethergarde engineer","nethergarde keep","nethergarde miner","stormwind"},rel={"subzone:nethergarde-keep","zone:blastedlands","topic:stormwind-kingdom","topic:alliance","topic:horde"},src={"Garrison Armory"}}
E["subzone:nethergarde-keep"] = {t="subzone",n="Nethergarde Keep",z="blastedlands",s="Nethergarde Keep is a fortified Alliance stronghold perched high upon the bluffs along the road entering the Blasted Lands. Erected by the Stonemasons Guild after the Second War, it stands as a vigilant sentinel over the dormant Dark Portal and the chaotic energies bleeding across the red wastes. Today, mages and garrisons supported by Stormwind continue their lonely vigil against demons and lingering corruption.",h="Nethergarde Keep is a fortified Alliance stronghold perched high upon the bluffs along the road entering the...",sec={{t="A Sentinel Against the Red World",b="Following the destruction of the Dark Portal at the end of the Second War, Archmage Khadgar and the leaders of the Alliance of Lordaeron recognized that Azeroth could never again leave the rift unguarded. Under the supervision of Edwin VanCleef, the Stonemasons Guild labored to raise towering bastions, barracks, and mage spires along the canyon pass into the Blasted Lands. Staffed by Kirin Tor sorcerers, its dual purpose was to keep constant watch on the shattered gateway and weave wards preventing the demonic blight of the scorched landscape from creeping northward into the human kingdoms.",sp=0},{t="The Lonely Vigil",b="When the Dark Portal reopened and the Alliance Expedition ventured into Draenor, Khadgar and his companions sealed the gateway behind them, leaving Nethergarde to guard a silent remnant. For two decades, scholars from Dalaran and the Wizard's Sanctum have analyzed the portal's lingering energies, mutated local fauna, and demonic incursions. With Dalaran ravaged during the Third War, Nethergarde relies entirely on vital supply caravans from Stormwind City to sustain its soldiers and mages as they stand alone against the horrors haunting the wasteland.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why was Nethergarde Keep built?",a="It was commissioned after the Second War by Archmage Khadgar and the Alliance of Lordaeron to guard against another orcish invasion from Draenor and contain the spreading demonic corruption of the Blasted Lands.",al={"purpose of nethergarde","why is nethergarde here","nethergarde history"}},{q="Who constructed the keep?",a="Nethergarde Keep was built by the Stonemasons Guild under the architectural direction of Edwin VanCleef, funded jointly by the member kingdoms of the Alliance of Lordaeron.",al={"who built nethergarde","nethergarde builders","vancleef nethergarde"}},{q="Who commands and supplies the fortress now?",a="Originally maintained by Dalaran's Kirin Tor, the fortress now relies primarily on the Kingdom of Stormwind for troops, regular supply caravans, and logistical support following Dalaran's fall to the Scourge and the Legion.",al={"who runs nethergarde","nethergarde supplies","stormwind nethergarde"}},{q="What are the mages inside the keep studying?",a="Researchers from the Wizard's Sanctum study the dormant energies of the Dark Portal, the strange mutations afflicting local wildlife, and methods to ward off the fel taint lingering over the red landscape.",al={"nethergarde mages","wizards sanctum nethergarde","what are they researching"}}},ang={["class:Mage"]="For practitioners of the arcane, Nethergarde represents decades of Kirin Tor research into dimensional rifts, rift sealing, and holding back the entropic spread of fel corruption.",["faction:Alliance"]="The fortress stands as one of the Alliance's most vital forward bulwarks, paid for in blood and gold to ensure the horrors of the First and Second Wars never spill out of the portal again."},kw={"blasted lands","dark portal","keep","khadgar","kirin tor","nethergarde","stonemasons","stormwind","vancleef"},rel={"subzone:dark-portal","zone:blastedlands","topic:stonemasons-guild","zone:stormwind","topic:second-war","topic:alliance-of-lordaeron","zone:swampofsorrows"},src={"Nethergarde Keep"}}
E["subzone:okril-lon-hold"] = {t="subzone",n="Okril'lon Hold",z="blastedlands",s="Perched in the northwestern crags of the Blasted Lands, this fortified stronghold was originally built by the Old Horde as Rockard during the First War. In the current era of 25 ADP, it is firmly occupied by the brutal Dreadmaul ogres under the name Dreadmaul Hold. The encampment serves as a fortified redoubt overlooking the scorched red plains below.",h="Perched in the northwestern crags of the Blasted Lands, this fortified stronghold was originally built by the...",sec={{t="From Rockard to Dreadmaul Hold",b="Long before the scorched expanse of the Blasted Lands emerged from the Black Morass, orcish invaders constructed Rockard alongside Stonard as one of the first settlements established on Azeroth after the Dark Portal opened. Though it survived the devastation of both the First and Second Wars, the departing orcs could not hold it. The Dreadmaul clan of ogres stormed the fortress, driving out any remaining defenders and claiming the stone towers and blacksmith for themselves. Renamed Dreadmaul Hold, it now serves as the primary garrison of the region's ogre population.",sp=0},{t="A Den of Ogre Supremacy",b="Under the iron rule of Grol the Destroyer, Dreadmaul Hold has become a nexus of brute force and dark allegiances. Enslaved or allied to the dreadlord Razelikh the Defiler, the ogres guard key mountain paths leading north toward the Swamp of Sorrows. Travelers and Horde supply trains skirting the northern mountains must remain ever vigilant against raiding warbands surging out of its gates.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is this place called Dreadmaul Hold instead of Okril'lon Hold?",a="In 25 ADP, the stronghold is known solely as Dreadmaul Hold. It was seized by the Dreadmaul ogres following the Second War.",al={"dreadmaul hold name","is this okrillon","why dreadmaul"}},{q="What was this settlement originally?",a="It was originally built as Rockard, an early outpost of the Old Horde established in the Black Morass shortly after the Dark Portal opened during the First War, making it one of the oldest orc settlements on Azeroth.",al={"who built this fortress","original name of dreadmaul hold","rockard history"}},{q="Who rules Dreadmaul Hold right now?",a="The hold is led by the ogre warlord Grol the Destroyer, who commands the Dreadmaul clan in the Blasted Lands and serves the demon Razelikh the Defiler.",al={"dreadmaul boss","who leads the ogres here","grol the destroyer"}},{q="Is the Horde in control of this base?",a="No. The fortress is entirely hostile to both the Horde and the Alliance, occupied solely by the Dreadmaul ogres.",al={"is dreadmaul horde","friendly base blasted lands"}}},ang={["race:Orc"]="Rockard was one of your people's earliest footholds on this world, and seeing it defiled and overrun by Dreadmaul ogres is a bitter reminder of the Old Horde's scattered collapse.",["faction:Alliance"]="Sitting right on the northern threshold of the Blasted Lands, the fortified hold represents a constant threat of ogre warbands ambushing patrols riding south from the Swamp of Sorrows."},kw={"black morass","blasted lands","dreadmaul hold","dreadmaul ogres","grol the destroyer","okril'lon hold","rockard"},rel={"zone:blastedlands","subzone:stonard","subzone:dark-portal","subzone:nethergarde-keep","npc:fallen-hero-of-the-horde","npc:loramus-thalipedes","topic:first-war","topic:second-war"},src={"Okril'lon Hold"}}
E["subzone:serpent-s-coil"] = {t="subzone",n="Serpent's Coil",z="blastedlands",s="Serpent's Coil is a winding network of caves and burnt-out encampments nestled in the eastern ridges of the Blasted Lands. Littered with scorched orcish architecture left behind from the older wars, it serves as a secluded redoubt for dark cultists and solitary researchers.",h="Serpent's Coil is a winding network of caves and burnt-out encampments nestled in the eastern ridges of the...",sec={{t="A Labyrinth of Ash and Stone",b="Carved into the jagged eastern cliffs of the Blasted Lands, the winding path and caverns of Serpent's Coil wind past ruined orcish huts that date back to the First and Second Wars. Rather than simple beasts, the tunnels harbor cabals of Shadowsworn cultists and practitioners of dark arts drawn to the residual demonic energies permeating the red wastes. Deep within its twisting hollows, odd figures pursue private obsessions far from the watchful eyes of Nethergarde Keep.",sp=0},{t="The Cultist Lair",b="The caverns have long served as a staging ground for Archmage Allistarj's cultists, who revere demonic lords and experiment with sinister artifacts like the Amulet of Allistarj. Even when their master's grasp wavers, loyal Shadowsworn zealots continue to patrol the cave turns, maintaining rituals in Kirith the Damned's service while hiding behind scorched barricades.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is Serpent's Coil?",a="Serpent's Coil is a winding cave network and canyon located in the eastern Blasted Lands, known for its charred orcish ruins and sinister occupants.",al={"serpents coil","what is this cave","blasted lands serpent coil"}},{q="Why are there old orc structures here?",a="The encampment structures date back to the First and Second Wars when the Old Horde crossed through the nearby Dark Portal and fortified the surrounding region before their defeat.",al={"why orc ruins","orc buildings blasted lands","burnt huts"}},{q="Who lives inside Serpent's Coil?",a="The caverns are occupied by Shadowsworn cultists aligned with Archmage Allistarj and dark powers, alongside isolated individuals studying the unusual magic of the Blasted Lands.",al={"who is here","serpent coil enemies","who controls the cave"}},{q="Why is there an Alliance gnome camped inside a cave surrounded by danger?",a="Kasim Sharim conducts private, dangerous magical research deep within the cavern, risking the surrounding cultists to study the potent demonic artifacts scattered throughout the territory.",al={"gnome in cave","kasim sharim","why is kasim here"}}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="The presence of a lone gnome researcher deep inside a cultist-infested cave exemplifies the fearless—or reckless—lengths gnomish intellect will go to unravel forbidden magic.",["class:Warlock"]="The Shadowsworn operating within Serpent's Coil practice binding rituals and harbor potent artifacts, making the cavern a grim reflection of reckless demonic study."},kw={"allistarj","blasted lands","kasim sharim","kirith the damned","serpent's coil","serpents coil","shadowsworn"},rel={"zone:blastedlands","topic:first-war","topic:second-war","topic:gnome","topic:horde","topic:alliance"},src={"Serpent's Coil"}}
E["subzone:tainted-scar"] = {t="subzone",n="Tainted Scar",z="blastedlands",s="The Tainted Scar is a demon-infested canyon carved into the southwestern Blasted Lands, saturated with foul fel magic from the nearby Dark Portal. It currently serves as the primary redoubt for the remnants of the Burning Legion on Azeroth, commanded by the doomguard Lord Kazzak.",h="The Tainted Scar is a demon-infested canyon carved into the southwestern Blasted Lands, saturated with foul...",sec={{t="A Bastion of the Legion",b="Once lush wetlands belonging to the ancient Black Morass, this desolate trench was utterly drained of life and turned the color of dried blood by chaotic fel energies leaking from the Dark Portal. Following Archimonde's defeat at Mount Hyjal during the Third War, surviving forces of the Burning Legion rallied in the south. The colossal ered'ruin Lord Kazzak claimed the Tainted Scar as his stronghold, stationing elite demons across its blackened rises and dispatching dreadful lieutenants like Razelikh the Defiler to hold dominion over the wasted red soils.",sp=0},{t="Unholy Inhabitants",b="While most mortals shun the Scar on pain of agonizing death, practitioners of the dark arts find its saturated fel energies irresistible. An eccentric human warlock named Daio the Decrepit has taken up residence by a ruined demonic altar overlooking the horrors, using the rampant fiends to perform dark rituals and instruct aspiring warlocks in how to summon and bind dread infernals.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Tainted Scar?",a="It is a canyon in the southwestern Blasted Lands heavily corrupted by demonic magic originating from the Dark Portal. Once part of the Black Morass, the land withered into a barren, blood-red wasteland populated almost entirely by high-ranking demons of the Burning Legion.",al={"what is tainted scar","tainted scar lore","why is the ground red here"}},{q="Who rules the Tainted Scar?",a="Lord Kazzak, a towering doomguard commander of the Burning Legion, oversees the demons gathered here. After the Legion's defeat in the Third War, he rallied the surviving fiends in the south to maintain a deadly foothold on Azeroth.",al={"who leads the demons here","tainted scar boss","lord kazzak tainted scar"}},{q="Why is an old human living among the demons here?",a="That hermit is Daio the Decrepit, an aged warlock who has braved the Scar to harness its potent fel ley energies. Rather than fleeing the demons, he conducts dark rituals at an altar here and mentors seasoned warlocks looking to master the summoning of infernals.",al={"who is daio","daio the decrepit","hermit in tainted scar"}},{q="Is the Tainted Scar connected to the Dark Portal?",a="Yes. When the Dark Portal first breached the boundary between worlds, chaotic Nether energies bled into the surrounding swamps. The Tainted Scar absorbed massive amounts of this magical fallout, permanently twisting the terrain into an inhospitable, demonic redoubt.",al={"tainted scar dark portal connection","why is it corrupted"}}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="The Tainted Scar is of great interest to veteran warlocks, who seek out Daio the Decrepit at his demonic altar to learn how to enslave and command fiery infernals.",["faction:Alliance"]="Alliance commanders closely monitor the canyon, fearful that Lord Kazzak's entrenched demon army could surge north into the Swamp of Sorrows or Stormwind territory."},kw={"blasted lands","burning legion","daio the decrepit","eredruin","kazzak","lord kazzak","razelikh","tainted scar"},rel={"zone:blastedlands","topic:burning-legion","subzone:dark-portal","topic:third-war","topic:alliance","topic:horde"},src={"Tainted Scar"}}
E["zone:blastedlands"] = {t="zone",n="Blasted Lands",z="blastedlands",s="The Blasted Lands are a desolate expanse of red clay and barren rock at the southeastern tip of the Eastern Kingdoms, ruined by the chaotic energies of the Dark Portal. Once part of the verdant Black Morass, the shattered earth now harbors demonic remnants of the Burning Legion, brutal Dreadmaul ogres, and hardy desert beasts. Nethergarde Keep stands vigil over the desolate wasteland, guarding Azeroth from whatever horrors may spill out of the dormant gateway.",h="The Blasted Lands are a desolate expanse of red clay and barren rock at the southeastern tip of the Eastern...",sec={{t="A Scarred Wasteland",b="Before the First War, this region was a continuation of the dense fenlands known as the Black Morass. That lush swamp was utterly eradicated when the warlock Gul'dan and the possessed Medivh tore open the Dark Portal to unleash the orcish Horde. Chaotic fel energies bled through the dimensional breach, stripping all moisture and baking the earth into cracked red clay. When the portal frame was later destroyed at the end of the Second War, catastrophic shockwaves scorched the terrain further, transmuting the native stone into its unearthly crimson hue.",sp=0},{t="Nethergarde's Lonely Vigil",b="Perched upon the northern bluffs, Nethergarde Keep watches over the only road entering the valley. Commissioned by Archmage Khadgar and the Kirin Tor following the Second War, this stone bastion is manned by grim mages and stalwart soldiers sworn to prevent any renewed demonic or orcish incursions. It is an uninviting and strictly disciplined posting; infractions among the garrison are punished with banishment to the Stockade in Stormwind. The defenders face relentless pressure from the Dreadmaul ogres who stayed behind after Draenor's fall, raiding the roads and attacking the fortress gates under fell guidance.",sp=0},{t="The Legion's Remnant",b="In the southwestern reaches lies the Tainted Scar, a cratered canyon teeming with the deadliest demonic force on the continent. Stranded after the defeat at Mount Hyjal, the doomguard commander Lord Kazzak gathers wandering demons, doomguard, and felhounds to his banner. High above the red barrens, his dreadlord lieutenant, Razelikh the Defiler, orchestrates mortal servitude among the Shadowsworn cultists at the Altar of Storms and commands the local Dreadmaul ogres.",sp=0},{t="The Power of the Blood",b="Despite the land's desolation, scholars and wanderers brave its horrors for unique discoveries. Just inside the northern pass, Bloodmage Drazial and Bloodmage Lynnore conduct eccentric alchemical experiments, extracting organs from local scorpids, basilisks, and boars to brew extraordinarily potent physical enhancers. Farther into the wastes, a lone draenei hermit named Kum'isha seeks scattered draenethyst fragments, rewarding travelers who recover these alien remnants left behind by Draenor's shattered past.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is the ground red and barren?",a="The Blasted Lands were once part of the marshy Black Morass. When the Dark Portal opened, raw demonic magic drained the region of life and moisture. When Khadgar later destroyed the portal's stone framework with the Skull of Gul'dan, the resulting catastrophic explosion seared the clay into hard crimson earth.",al={"why is blasted lands red","why is it dead","what happened to the swamp"}},{q="What is the Dark Portal?",a="The Dark Portal is a massive dimensional gateway constructed to link Azeroth to Draenor, the sundered homeworld of the orcs now known as Outland. Though its stone frame was shattered to sever the bridge between worlds, the focal rift remains, guarded perpetually by Nethergarde Keep.",al={"where does dark portal go","is the portal open","what is the gateway"}},{q="Who controls Nethergarde Keep?",a="Nethergarde Keep is an Alliance bastion overseen by mages of the Kirin Tor and soldiers loyal to Stormwind. Built after the Second War under Archmage Khadgar's direction, its garrison maintains a strictly disciplined, dour watch over the Dark Portal and repels nearby ogre and demon attacks.",al={"who runs nethergarde","is nethergarde alliance","nethergarde mages"}},{q="What is the Tainted Scar?",a="The Tainted Scar is a demon-infested canyon in the southern Blasted Lands. It serves as a refuge for the remaining forces of the Burning Legion in the Eastern Kingdoms, spearheaded by the powerful doomguard Lord Kazzak and populated by doomguards, felguards, and felhounds.",al={"tainted scar elite area","who is in tainted scar","demon valley blasted lands"}},{q="Who are the blood elves camping near the entrance?",a="Bloodmage Drazial and Bloodmage Lynnore are researchers studying how the corrupted fauna adapted to the harsh fel landscape. In exchange for the entrails, brains, and lungs of native basilisks, vultures, scorpids, and boars, they brew powerful singular elixirs that bolster mortal attributes.",al={"blood elf buff potions","drazial and lynnore","boar lung quest"}},{q="Who is Kum'isha the Collector?",a="Kum'isha is an enigmatic draenei mystic dwelling in the central wastes. He collects draenethyst fragments and spheres—crystalline remnants originating from Draenor—and trades sealed packs of rare equipment and goods to anyone who brings them to him.",al={"draenei in blasted lands","kumisha","draenethyst quest"}},{q="How do you reach the Blasted Lands on foot?",a="Travel through Deadwind Pass east into the Swamp of Sorrows. From the Swamp of Sorrows, follow the primary road southward past the Horde settlement of Stonard until you reach the narrow mountain pass leading directly onto the red clay of the Blasted Lands.",al={"getting to blasted lands","how to get there","blasted lands entrance"}},{q="Why are there ogres living in the desert?",a="The Dreadmaul ogres crossed through the Dark Portal during the Second War. Rather than retreating back through the rift, they entrenched themselves within Dreadmaul Hold and fell under the thrall of the dreadlord Razelikh and the Shadowsworn cult.",al={"dreadmaul ogres lore","why are ogres here","dreadmaul hold"}}},ang={["class:Mage"]="The mages of Nethergarde Keep embody the stern, defensive application of the arcane, holding vigil against fel corruption and dimensional rifts left by Medivh's fall.",["class:Warlock"]="With the Tainted Scar swarming with high-ranking demons and Daio the Decrepit dwelling among the rocks, this desolate land offers seasoned warlocks unprecedented opportunities to bind dangerous fel entities.",["profession:Herbalism"]="The arid red clay is one of the extremely rare natural environments where Gromsblood grows, sprouted from ancient drops of demonic blood spilled upon the earth.",["faction:Alliance"]="Nethergarde Keep stands as your sole fortified haven in the region, guarding the southern reaches of the kingdom from horrors that could threaten Duskwood and Stormwind.",["faction:Horde"]="Though the Horde maintains no fortress here, the ruins of the Dark Portal serve as a grim monument to the Old Horde's crossing and the devastation wrought by demonic corruption."},kw={"black morass","blasted lands","dark portal","drazial","dreadmaul","gromsblood","kum'isha","lord kazzak","lynnore","nethergarde keep","razelikh","tainted scar"},rel={"subzone:dark-portal","subzone:nethergarde-keep","subzone:tainted-scar","zone:swampofsorrows","npc:bloodmage-drazial","npc:bloodmage-lynnore","subzone:altar-of-storms-burning-steppes"},src={"Blasted Lands (Classic)","Blasted Lands"}}
